For GW170817, the chirp mass of the system is precisely constrained to 1.188^{+0.004}_{-0.002} M{}_{\\odot}. On the other hand, for a wide range of NS EOSs, the dynamical ejecta mass is essentially determined by the mass ratio of the two NSs. In order to be as comprehensive as possible, we employ 38 representative microphysical EoSs4, which are derived in Bauswein et al. (2012) and Bauswein et al. (2013), within different theoretical frameworks, including nonrelativistic and relativistic nuclear energy-density functionals, Brueckner-Hartree-Fock calcula

